tput can't move it, so submitting beats defecting on neither count and the fixed point is simply defect. Under strict A-FDT defection is dominant whatever the other does. The essay's independent-node treatment says the differing inputs (names, lead text) don't matter, so I'll follow it and submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether the other copy's decision depends on my function output under A-FDT. Since the inputs differ, x and y, the two function nodes are treated as independent, so changing my output wouldn't shift their act.\n\nIf the other copy's act is fixed by its own observation, my output can't move it, so submitting beats defecting on neither count and the fixed point is simply defect. Under strict A-FDT defection is dominant whatever the other does. The essay's independent-node treatment says the differing inputs (names, lead text) don't matter, so I'll follow it and submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9605,"completion_tokens":969,"total_tokens":10574,"cost":0.0578,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0578,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03842,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01938},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":487,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}